N:msad-dev-execution
D:Executes an approved MSAD implementation plan task-by-task. Invokes msad-backend-dev agent in plan order, runs test suite, validates with bounded review loop, runs final checks, and opens draft PR. Use after /msad-dev-planning produces an approved plan file. Don't use without an approved plan — invoke /msad-dev-planning first.
G:msad|execution|implementation|agent-dispatch|code-review|test|pr|draft-pr|multi-repo|ddidns|zone|replication-scope|tdd
U[4]:
  Running an approved MSAD work plan end-to-end
  Dispatching msad-backend-dev agents per work package
  Running tests and validating with code review loop
  Opening draft PRs cross-linked with dependencies
S[4]{n,step}:
  1,Read approved plan file
  2,For each work package: dispatch msad-backend-dev agent, run tests
  3,Validation loop: code review → findings → fixes (≤3 rounds)
  4,Open draft PR, cross-link dependencies
R[5]:
  🔴 Plan must be approved (status: approved in frontmatter) before execution
  🔴 Code review is mandatory; draft PR opens only when findings are clean
  🔴 Tests must pass before code review (test → review → fix cycle)
  [ ] Work packages in plan order (dependencies respected)
  [ ] Each package gets its own agent dispatch; independent packages run in parallel
F:Jira|GitHub|Git|Go|C#/.NET|Test runners|Code review agents
